        <name>DsiPath_Init</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>One-time DSI TX Subsystem + ATtiny MCU + ILI9881C panel bring-up. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Must be called once at boot, regardless of whether DSI or HDMI is the initially selected output — this brings the panel up in COMMAND mode and leaves the DSI TX Subsystem configured for VIDEO mode at the panel&apos;s native 720x1280 timing, ready for DsiPath_StartVideo() to activate it.</para><para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS or XST_FAILURE.</para></simplesect>
See dsi_txss_display.h for the split rationale vs DsiPath_StartVideo(). </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
