      <memberdef kind="function" id="xmipi__scu200__xp5io__example_2dsi__txss__display_8h_1ac8c31c00913fa51695ad87917187a665" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void DsiPath_Reinit</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>DsiPath_Reinit</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Hardware-reset the DSI TX Subsystem (XDsiTxSs_Reset()) and re-apply its VIDEO mode timing configuration, without starting it. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Call this every time DSI is about to become (or stop being) the active output — after DsiPath_StopVideo(), before DsiPath_StartVideo(). Recovers the core from having starved on a cut-off AXI4-Stream input, which a bare Activate(DISABLE)/(ENABLE) toggle alone does not reliably do.</para><para>Hardware-reset the DSI TX Subsystem (XDsiTxSs_Reset()) and re-apply its VIDEO mode timing configuration, without starting it.</para><para>Matches the ZCU102 reference&apos;s <ref refid="function__prototype_8c_1a571466dbec30928cd622090965a7ef0f" kindref="member">InitDSI()</ref>: a bare XDsiTxSs_Activate(DISABLE)/(ENABLE) toggle is not sufficient to recover the core from having starved on a cut-off AXI4- Stream input (proven empirically — that approach was tried and caused a FIFO under-run on the very first switch to DSI). XDsiTxSs_Reset() clears the byte-stream FIFO and protocol engine state at the register level, so the core comes back in the same known-good state it was in right after boot, instead of whatever state a starve event left it in.</para><para>Call this every time DSI is about to become (or stop being) the active output, before DsiPath_StartVideo() — never call DsiPath_StartVideo() without a preceding DsiPath_Reinit() once the core has ever been disabled/starved. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
